---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const html = '<p>People want a table. Here is one, labeled the only honest way: <strong>illustrative 2026 ranges, not IRS limits and not a Savant quote.</strong> They assume durable compensation near the <strong>$360,000</strong> cap, a retirement age around 62, a fixed interest credit, and no expensive staff. Change any of those and the deposit moves.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Around age 40: often a six-figure credit, commonly discussed in a <strong>$100,000 to $140,000</strong> illustrative band.</li>\n<li>Around age 50: often nearer <strong>$180,000 to $230,000</strong>, illustrative.</li>\n<li>Around age 55: often <strong>$240,000 to $290,000</strong>, illustrative.</li>\n<li>Around age 60: sometimes above <strong>$300,000</strong>, illustrative, because fewer years remain under the <strong>$290,000</strong> benefit ceiling.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The benefit ceiling itself is statutory. The deposit is not. Confirm the ceiling on the <a href="https://www.irs.gov/retirement-plans/plan-participant-employee/retirement-topics-defined-benefit-plan-benefit-limits">IRS page</a> and the paired 401(k) limits in <a href="https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/401k-limit-increases-to-24500-for-2026-ira-limit-increases-to-7500">IR-2025-111</a>. A worked comparison with a SEP is on <a href="/compare">compare</a>. The <a href="/calculator">calculator</a> on this site is a conversation starter with the same warning. For a number you can hand a CPA, we need a census and an Enrolled Actuary. <a href="/contact">That is the next step</a>.</p>';
---
<Base title="What an age table is, and is not. | Savant Pensions">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <p class="kicker">Illustrations</p>
    <h1>Illustrative cash balance contributions.</h1>
    <p class="lede">These ranges are sketches. Your number comes from a census and an actuary.</p>
    <div class="guide" set:html={html} />
  </section>
</Base>
